    rdfs:comment "https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Wikidata:Licensing — \"All structured data (i.e. the main, Property, Lexeme, and EntitySchema namespaces) is released into the public domain under Creative Commons Zero.\""@en .

<https://en.wikisource.org/wiki/1911_Encyclop%C3%A6dia_Britannica>
    dcterms:title "Encyclopædia Britannica, 11th edition (1911): the articles on the Swedish kings (Gustavus I. Eriksson to Gustavus V.) and \"Sweden\" (History), as transcribed on Wikisource" ;
    dcterms:creator "Robert Nisbet Bain (the articles on the kings from Gustavus I. to Charles XV., except Oscar I.); Oscar I., Oscar II. and Gustavus V. unsigned; \"Sweden\" by Frederick Beck, Robert Nisbet Bain, Oskar Dumrath, Osbert Howarth and Edmund Gosse; transcribed by Wikisource contributors" ;
    rdfs:comment "https://en.wikisource.org/wiki/1911_Encyclop%C3%A6dia_Britannica — licence box: \"This work is in the public domain in the United States because it was published before January 1, 1931.\" Most of the articles on the individual kings name Robert Nisbet Bain (1854–1909) as contributor in their Wikisource header (e.g. https://en.wikisource.org/wiki/1911_Encyclop%C3%A6dia_Britannica/Gustavus_III.?action=raw: \"|contributor = Robert Nisbet Bain\"), so they are out of copyright under life-plus-70 terms as well; \"Oscar I.\", \"Oscar II.\" and \"Gustavus V.\" have no contributor field (unsigned), and as anonymous works published in 1910–1911 they are out of copyright under publication-based terms too. Only facts were taken, in the compiler's own words."@en .

